[center][size=6][b]OVERLAY MAP[/b][/size]
[size=4]A hologram world map that opens over the game with one key.
Built to be lightweight, so you can use it without pausing your gameplay.[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What it is[/b][/size]
The vanilla map pauses the game and takes over the screen. Overlay Map is a 2D map of the whole city that opens as a hologram panel right where you are, while the world keeps moving behind it. Check where you are, find the next gig, set a waypoint and close it again, without ever leaving the street.

It draws the vanilla map's own roads and buildings, shows the game's markers with their vanilla icons, and mirrors your GPS routes.

[line]

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[b]The map[/b]
[list]
[*][b]The whole city.[/b] Roads and buildings come from the game's own map data, Dogtown and the Badlands included.
[*][b]Zoom from a street corner to all of Night City.[/b] A scale bar shows the distance at every zoom level.
[*][b]Follows V.[/b] The map stays centred on V until you pan away; one key brings it back.
[*][b]Area names.[/b] The sidebar names the area and district under the cursor, in your game language.
[*][b]NCART lines.[/b] An optional filter draws the five metro lines in their own colours.
[/list]

[b]Markers and navigation[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Vanilla markers.[/b] Quests, gigs, cyberpsycho sightings, NCPD hustles, fast travel, ripperdocs, vendors, autofixers, drop points, apartments and more, with the game's own icons. Minor markers fade out as you zoom out, so the far view stays readable; the tracked quest and V never do.
[*][b]Marker details.[/b] Put a marker near the centre and the sidebar shows what it is, where it is and how far away.
[*][b]Quick filter.[/b] One key cycles the markers shown: All, Jobs, Services.
[*][b]Waypoints.[/b] E works like right-clicking on the vanilla map: set a custom waypoint on an empty spot, make a job active, track a marker, or clear what you're tracking.
[*][b]GPS routes.[/b] Your waypoint route (white) and the tracked quest's route (yellow, teal for gigs) are drawn as flowing dots.
[*][b]Fast travel and teleport.[/b] Fast travel from any fast travel marker the game's way, or teleport V (and V's car) to any spot on the map.
[/list]

[b]Collectibles and photos[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Collectibles.[/b] Every shard, tarot graffiti, iconic weapon, legendary cyberware and clothing piece, and skill shard placed in the world gets its own pin. Collected ones stay on the map, scratched out, so you can see what's left.
[*][b]Photo pins.[/b] Photos you take in photo mode are pinned where you took them, with a thumbnail on the map and in the sidebar, and kept between sessions. Teleport back to any of them.
[/list]

[b]Look[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Five colour themes:[/b] Cyan, Red, Green, Purple and Amber, or follow your HUD Painter colours.
[*][b]Hologram style:[/b] glowing roads, scanlines, a grid and an edge glow, with an optional VHS tracking band and glitch. Or switch the effects off for a plain, clean map.
[/list]

[b]Controls[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Keyboard and mouse, numpad or controller.[/b] All three work, and every key can be rebound.
[*][b]Open it your way:[/b] a single key, a combo such as Ctrl + M, or hold the key to show the map only while it's held.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Controls[/b][/size]
[b]O[/b] opens and closes the map (it does nothing in menus or photo mode).

[b]Keyboard and mouse (default).[/b] While the map is open it takes the keyboard and mouse, and V stands still:
[list]
[*]Pan: [b]move the mouse[/b], or W A S D / the arrow keys
[*]Zoom: mouse wheel
[*]Follow V again: Space
[*]Act on the selected marker: F
[*]Set waypoint / track: E or Enter
[*]Teleport / fast travel: Q
[*]Cycle marker filter: R
[/list]

[b]Numpad.[/b] With [i]Controls[/i] set to [i]Numpad[/i], the map uses only the numpad, so you keep full control of V's movement and the mouse while it's open. Numpad 8 4 6 2 pan (7 9 1 3 diagonally), + and − zoom, 5 follows V, 0 acts, Enter sets a waypoint, / cycles the filter, . teleports. Keep NumLock on.

[b]Mouse only.[/b] With [i]Controls[/i] set to [i]Mouse only[/i], you keep walking or driving with the keyboard while the mouse drives the map: move it to pan, wheel to zoom, left click acts, hold left click for 2 seconds to teleport (a ring fills around the crosshair), right click sets a waypoint.

[b]Controller.[/b] Hold View for half a second to open the map (a tap still opens the pause menu). Left stick pans, LT/RT zoom, A acts, RB sets a waypoint, X teleports, Y cycles the filter, R3 follows V, B closes.

[line]

[size=5][b]Make it yours[/b][/size]
Everything is in [b]Mod Settings → Overlay Map[/b]. The most useful options:

[b]Keys[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Open / close map[/b] and [b]Open map modifier:[/b] pick any key, and add Shift, Ctrl or both for a combo such as Ctrl + M. The key alone closes the map.
[*][b]Controls[/b] (the first setting): [i]WASD[/i] (V stands still, WASD and the mouse drive the map), [i]Numpad[/i] (V keeps full control; the map uses the numpad) or [i]Mouse only[/i] (V keeps walking and driving; the mouse drives the map).
[*][b]Mouse pans the map[/b] and [b]Mouse pan speed:[/b] on by default. Switch it off to keep turning the camera with the mouse while the map is open.
[*][b]Open map button[/b] (Controller): hold View to open, or turn the controller shortcut off.
[/list]

[b]Display[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Hologram colour:[/b] Cyan, Green, Red, Purple or Amber.
[*][b]Map size:[/b] make the panel smaller if you want more of the world in view.
[*][b]Panel opacity[/b] and [b]Map opacity:[/b] how much of the world shows through the panel, or through the whole map.
[*][b]Map brightness[/b] and [b]Map contrast:[/b] make the roads and buildings brighter, dimmer or stand out more.
[*][b]Map marker size:[/b] bigger or smaller markers.
[*][b]Hologram effects:[/b] the grid, scanlines and animations; off gives a plain background. [b]Scanline strength[/b] and [b]Glow strength[/b] fine-tune them, and [b]VHS tracking band[/b] and [b]VHS glitch[/b] add a worn-tape look.
[*][b]Hide HUD while open:[/b] fade the game's HUD while the map is up, or keep it.
[*][b]Hold key to show:[/b] the map stays up only while the open key is held.
[*][b]Teleport key:[/b] switch teleporting off if you'd rather not have it.
[*][b]GPS routes[/b] and [b]Photo pins:[/b] show or hide them.
[*][b]Follow HUD Painter colours:[/b] take the map's colours from your HUD Painter preset.
[/list]

[b]Map filters[/b]
[list]
[*]Turn each marker category on or off: jobs, gigs, cyberpsychos, NCPD, fast travel, ripperdocs, vendors, autofixers, drop points, apartments for rent, tarot, and your own apartments and vehicles.
[*][b]NCART lines:[/b] off by default; turn it on to see the metro.
[/list]

[b]Collectibles[/b]
[list]
[*]Turn each type on or off: shards, tarot, iconic weapons, cyberware, clothing, skill shards.
[*][b]Show collected:[/b] keep collected ones on the map scratched out, or hide them.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 [b]2.5[/b]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url]
[/list]
[b]Optional:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], for the settings menu and key rebinding. Without it every option keeps its default.

[line]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with Vortex or Mod Organizer 2, or unzip into your Cyberpunk 2077 folder (the one with [i]bin[/i], [i]archive[/i] and [i]r6[/i]).

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete these three:
[list]
[*]archive/pc/mod/OverlayMap.archive
[*]r6/scripts/OverlayMap/
[*]red4ext/plugins/OverlayMapNative/
[/list]
Your photo pins are kept in r6/storages/OverlayMap/; delete that folder too to remove them.

[line]

[size=5][b]Known issues[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Waypoints and saving new photo pins use the mod's small RED4ext plugin, tested on game 2.5. If a game update leaves it unable to find the game function it needs, those two switch off and everything else keeps working.
[*]The game's HUD fades out while the map is open. Display → [i]Hide HUD while open[/i] turns that off.
[*]On a game version other than 2.5 the map shows a notice that some places may not match.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]For mod authors[/b][/size]
Other mods can add their own items to the map through a layer API. Ask in the comments if you'd like to use it.

If you like my mods and want to support me, please buy me a coffee at [url=https://ko-fi.com/pointdotpoint]https://ko-fi.com/pointdotpoint[/url]
